
LiveStage appliance (Alpine Linux)

  livestage-setup                               name, network, Wi-Fi, interface, password
  rc-service livestage restart | stop | start   the mixer
  tail -f /var/log/livestage.log                its log
  livestage-server --list-devices               audio interfaces
  aplay -l                                      ALSA cards

  Setup:         /var/lib/livestage/setup.conf  (livestage-setup writes it)
  Settings:      /var/lib/livestage/livestage.conf  (see /etc/conf.d/livestage)
  Session:       /data/livestage/show.json  (exFAT: readable on any computer)
  Recordings:    /data/livestage/recordings, or a USB drive's
                 "LiveStage Recordings" (Setup → Storage)
  Storage log:   /var/log/livestage-storage.log

  The system is read-only. To change it: mount -o remount,rw /

